00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.310
There are three types of audit
logs that we may be discussing,

00:01:32.310 --> 00:01:33.930
or will be discussing.

00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:37.140
The first is admin
activity audit logs.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.490
Now, these are always on
and always free for the GCP

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:42.990
services that produce them.

00:01:42.990 --> 00:01:45.570
And they tell you about
the creation and deletion

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:48.190
of resources.

00:01:48.190 --> 00:01:51.720
The second type of audit logs
is data access audit logs.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:54.330
These logs tell you about
data reading and writing

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.640
and you must turn them on.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:59.190
If you think about your
usage of the cloud,

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:01.830
you read and write data a lot
more than you create and delete

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.070
resources.

00:02:03.070 --> 00:02:04.860
So these logs may
be very high volume,

00:02:04.860 --> 00:02:06.401
and we'll talk a
little bit about how

00:02:06.401 --> 00:02:08.639
to manage that volume.

00:02:08.639 --> 00:02:13.020
And the third type of audit logs
is access transparency logs.

00:02:13.020 --> 00:02:16.470
And these tell you when Google
support or Google engineers

00:02:16.470 --> 00:02:18.810
access your resources.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.610
These logs must
also be turned on,

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:24.810
and they're available to
platinum and gold customers.

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:27.060
Just a little note
on retention--

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:31.140
admin activity audit logs
are retained for 400 days.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:33.480
Data access and access
transparency audit logs

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.010
are retained for 30 days.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:37.080
And we'll show you how
to set up longer term

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:41.260
storage for your logs
as part of this talk.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:43.630
So what are we going
to cover today?

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:46.110
